From 951f8e35cfaa5016458f304af82c7c6c33fc81bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yichao Yu <yyc1992@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:17:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] slsqp: detect BLAS/LAPACK at configure time, with a
 built-in fallback

New CMake option NLOPT_BLAS (case-insensitive): AUTO (default) uses a
BLAS/LAPACK found by FindLAPACK if it provides the routines SLSQP needs,
ON requires one, OFF never uses one, and any other value is passed as
the library list (names, paths or flags) to link against.  The Fortran
symbol suffix ("_64_", "_64", "_" or none) is found by test-linking all
17 routines, without running anything, so this works when
cross-compiling; a "64" suffix means 64-bit integers.  Libraries that
provide both interfaces get the one matching the pointer size.  The
libraries are added to Libs.private in nlopt.pc.

Without a BLAS/LAPACK, slsqp_blas.h provides plain C ports of the
reference BLAS/LAPACK 3.12 routines that SLSQP calls (pointer-sized
integers), restricted to the arguments used: DGELSY without column
pivoting (SLSQP fixes all columns) and with the basic instead of the
minimum-norm solution when rank deficient (SLSQP then stops with an
error and uses only the rank).  Compared with OpenBLAS on random inputs
they agree to rounding and make the same rank decisions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
